Two Features of a Stock Audit Relevant to Inventory Management

1. Physical Stock Verification

This involves comparing the actual quantity of items in storage with the quantity recorded in the inventory system. It helps identify shortages, excess stock, damaged goods, theft, and recording errors.

2. Inventory Reconciliation and Variance Reporting

This involves identifying and recording differences between the expected and actual stock levels, investigating the causes, and correcting the inventory records. It helps improve stock accuracy and supports proper purchasing and replenishment decisions.
